    "type": "question",
    "label": "11",
    "prompt": "A mound of earth is shaped like a cone. It is 6 metres high with a radius of 25 metres. Find the cost, to the nearest dollar, of moving the mound if it costs $\\$5$ to move one cubic metre.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\$19\\,635$",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}V&=\\frac13\\pi r^2h\\\\V&=\\frac13\\pi\\times25^2\\times6\\\\V&=1250\\pi\\,\\mathrm{m}^{3}.\\end{align*}$$\nAt $\\$5$ per cubic metre:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Cost}&=5\\times1250\\pi\\\\\\text{Cost}&=6250\\pi\\\\\\text{Cost}&\\approx\\$19\\,635\\quad\\text{(nearest dollar).}\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
